  "note": "ADR 0016 Shelf-B `lists` bundle v1.1.0 — the COMPLETE relational list library over CONS-CELL lists (`[H|T]` = Tuple[Atom('.'), H, T]; nil = Atom('[]')). SUPERSET of lists@1.0.0 (issue #240): it RE-INCLUDES `append/3` + `length/2` BYTE-IDENTICALLY (same clauses, same ClauseId::canonical — `append`: 1a5ba4ff…, 19509a05…; `length`: a801e66e…, 00db4fb5…) and ADDS the standard relations `member/2`, `reverse/2`, `nth0/3`, `last/2` (issue #242). These are ordinary account `Rule` nodes the EXISTING check() verifies as §7 dual-conformance derivations — ZERO new trusted code, no account node kind, no dependency on #159 list reification (the Shelf-A reified `ListTheory` over the list() embedding stays DEFERRED → #277). lists@1.0.0.json is UNCHANGED and stays byte-pinned by its own differential vector; 1.1.0 is a NEW, additive bundle (Shelf B is byte-frozen per name@version). Each relation is range-restricted, safe, and terminating: `member(X,[X|_]).` / `member(X,[_|T]):-member(X,T).`; `reverse` uses an accumulator (`reverse(L,R):-rev_(L,[],R). rev_([],A,A). rev_([H|T],A,R):-rev_(T,[H|A],R).`); `nth0` is 0-indexed via a counting accumulator over the FROZEN ontos/data `int` embedding (`nth0(I,L,X):-nth0_(L,int(0),I,X). nth0_([H|_],I,I,H). nth0_([_|T],I0,I,X):-I1 is I0+int(1), nth0_(T,I1,I,X).`) so it is multi-directional (index→element AND enumerate-index); `last([X],X). last([_|T],X):-last(T,X).`. `length`/`nth0` count with `is/2` over the §5.1 `int` embedding (`int(N)` = Tuple[Atom('int'), Atom(<sign||be-magnitude>)]); the int payloads here are int(0)=atom 00, int(1)=atom 0001 (sign byte 0x00 then big-endian minimal magnitude). NOTE the structure-only relations (`member`/`reverse`/`last` and the `append`/3 split) need NO theory — they resolve by unification alone; only `length`/`nth0` invoke the ArithmeticTheory's `is/2`. `program_digest` = lowercase-hex SHA-256(PROGRAM_PREFIX 'logos/account/program/v1\\n' || concat of len-prefixed SORTED ontos-codec(quote(clause-as-term)) bytes), recomputed and verified by load_prelude. Each clause `id` = ClauseId::canonical. Term notation as in vectors/account.json: term = {atom:<hex>}|{atom_str:<utf8>}|{tuple:[...]}|{var:<id>}; goal = {pred:<utf8>, args:[term...]}; negated body literal = {neg:<goal>}.",
